# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
# Real static files (and /assets/*) are served first and take precedence, and
# functions/_middleware.js runs ahead of this for every included route (proxy,
# slug-redirect, SEO injection). This rule applies when the static layer would
# otherwise 404 — i.e. a client-side route like /article/<slug> with no matching
# file — so the SPA shell (index.html) is returned with a 200 instead of a 404.
# Keeps SPA routing consistent on Pages.
#
# NOTE: a missing /assets/<oldhash>.js (after a deploy) also falls through to
# this rule and gets index.html + 200, which the client's retryImport.ts
# classifies as a MIME/CORS chunk failure → deployRecovery reload. The proactive
# buildVersion poll (client/src/lib/buildVersion.ts) prevents the stale-tab case
# in the first place by reloading before a deleted chunk is ever requested.
/*    /index.html   200
